        "# Peak Finding Challenge"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8aubqUmimNwd"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In this in-class activity, you will adjust parameters on SciPy's automated \"find_peaks\" function to adequately identify peaks in a set of IR spectra. Polymer datasets are taken from O. Villegas-Camacho et. al. \"FTIR-Plastics: A Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy dataset for the six most prevalent inducstrial plastic polymers\", *Data in Brief* 55, 110612 (2024) https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dib.2024.110612"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "lzCJWJt3mTDU"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "<font size=4>Goals: By the end of this activity you should:  \n",
        "1. Be familiar with an example of algorithmic thinking and translating logic to code using natural language  \n",
        "2. Be able to identify functional groups within molecules using FTIR peak positions  \n",
        "3. Find peaks and adjust parameters in scipy's \"find_peaks\" function to optimally find the peaks you want  \n",
        "4. Identify places where code may fail and suggest improvements  \n",
        "From a Python perspective, pay attention to:  \n",
        "  - f-strings\n",
        "  - Pandas dataframes"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "v5k113w0Uy_h"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Imports"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7zKRp-UxnJ8M"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
