    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "pname = # insert your string here\n",
        "\n",
        "pol1 = pd.read_csv(f'{dpath}{pname}1.csv',skiprows=15,header=None,names=['wavenumber','intensity'])\n",
        "pol2 = pd.read_csv(f'{dpath}{pname}2.csv',skiprows=15,header=None,names=['wavenumber','intensity'])\n",
        "pol3 = pd.read_csv(f'{dpath}{pname}3.csv',skiprows=15,header=None,names=['wavenumber','intensity'])"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3-maKlB5No6r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The data is given in transmission; for peaks, let's convert to absorbance. We'll add a third column to the pandas dataframe.  \n",
        "$A = log_{10}(\\frac{1}{T})$  \n",
        "To do this, we are using one of the previous columns."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9xk1H1HCOB3p"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "pol1.insert(2, \"Abs\", np.log10(1/pol1['intensity']))\n",
        "pol2.insert(2, \"Abs\", np.log10(1/pol2['intensity']))\n",
        "pol3.insert(2, \"Abs\", np.log10(1/pol3['intensity']))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "aPFEEKDuFMA-"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Take a look at the structure of the dataframe:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "X-1oF8AJP9gi"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "pol1"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "quhU2a9ZQAEU"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Now, we'll make two side-by-side plots to see the transformation. Note that we have set the wavenumbers going from high to low, as is generally convention."
